        <!-- ============ KEY DISTINCTION NOTE ============ -->
        <mxCell id="note" value="KEY DISTINCTION&#10;&#10;â€¢ Resolver ENDPOINTS (inbound / outbound) are PLACED in ONE VPC&#10;   via subnet ENIs. You don't 'associate' them, can't move them,&#10;   can't share them, and they don't span VPCs.&#10;&#10;â€¢ Resolver RULES and PRIVATE HOSTED ZONES are ASSOCIATED to&#10;   many VPCs, and shared via RAM / Route 53 Profiles.&#10;&#10;â€¢ A FORWARD rule REFERENCES an outbound endpoint as its target." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fillColor=#FFF9E6;strokeColor=#D6B656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
